  "body": "## What (closes the MVP definition in plan \u00a73)\n- **PRs screen is live**: `LiveSource` runs `prs::repos_from_board` + `prs::list` on a background thread every 60 s (first snapshot waits \u2264 1.5 s so `BF_TUI_ONCE`/piped frames carry real counts; the loader stays under 2 s), maps `Pr \u2192 PrRow` including the exact missing merge preconditions, and on failure keeps the last rows and sets `prs_stale_since` (RFC3339 of the last good fetch, or `never`) \u2192 status line `gh unavailable: PRs stale since \u2026`.\n- **Transcript tail in the Agents detail**: last 64 KiB of the transcript, partial first line dropped, last 40 messages as `role: text` (\u2264 200 chars, through `terminal_text`); parsers for the Claude, Codex, Cursor and Grok line shapes (unit-tested against real shapes from this host); cached by (path, mtime, len) with a 60 ms per-snapshot read budget so 30+ agents never stall the screen. Claude registry rows are resolved to `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/<session>.jsonl`; Codex/Cursor/Grok tails need discovery to expose their paths (follow-up on PR #5).\n- `tests/cli_polish.rs`: claim in a repo whose origin is `neverhuman/fixture-a`, then `BF_TUI_ONCE=1 bf` under the fake `gh` shim \u2192 status line `PRs 2 open`, first frame < 2 s; with `gh` failing \u2192 `PRs 0 open` + `gh unavailable: PRs stale since never`. 4 unit tests + one `#[ignore]` bench in `live.rs`.\n\nFiles: `src/live.rs`, `tests/cli_polish.rs`. No tui/, agents.rs, prs.rs or Cargo changes; no new deps.\n\n## Evidence (this host, 17:20Z)\nfmt/clippy `-D warnings` clean; 54 tests green (lib 24, cli_polish 1, cli_agents 2, cli_board 2, cli_prs 5, cli_skeleton 5, cli_wiring 3, core 3, tui 8); `bash scripts/check` EXIT 0 in 17 s. `BF_TUI_ONCE=1 bf` \u2192 `bf \u00b7 agents 34 (claude 7 codex 18 grok 7 cursor 2) \u00b7 busy 3 \u00b7 claims 1 \u00b7 PRs 0` in 0.79 s wall (gh answered in ~0.5 s). Bench: first snapshot 0.7 s incl. gh wait; steady state \u2248 `bf agents` alone (~0.2 s debug); worst case 32 fresh transcript tails 0.2 s, capped by the 60 ms budget per snapshot.\n\n## Review\nReviewer must be a different vendor (grok, codex or cursor): `REVIEW: approve <head-sha>` via `gh pr review --comment`, then `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch`.\n\nbf-author: claude/claude-orch \u00b7 bf-claim: c-4\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
